A||||8||Greg Piet||What about the mid-engine?||||1
Z||000000||Greg Piet||09-20-1999||07:52 PM||||I was reading through the stories about why everone bought their Fiero's.<BR>I rarely saw anyone mentioning that the mid engine was one of the reasons for buying one.<P>Unlike Cliff, I am a huge Porsche and VW beetle enthusiast, and one reason for this is that the engine is behind the driver.<P>Is anyone else out there loving the fiero for the motor being behind the driver?||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GT||09-20-1999||08:28 PM||||I kind of like the engine being behind me so that I can hear every little noise is makes. lol!  The only thing I dont like about it being in back is that the front of the car is a lot lighter.  I always have to take it real easy on wet roads.  When I had my 94 Grand Prix, I could go through puddles without thinking about it.  But, with my Fiero, I have to pay a lot of attention. lol! Other than that, its fun to drive.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||09-20-1999||10:35 PM||||The mid engine was one part of the whole unique Fiero design that I liked. Styling, plastic body, and handling (partly due to mid engine) were also considerations swaying me to buy my first one. They just look damn good...ya know what I mean!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 09-20-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||biggdaddy||09-20-1999||11:09 PM||||I too am a huge PORSCHE fan.  But what Porsche do you like that sports a mid-engine.  Rear-engine, but not mid-engine, there is a big difference.  Plus, the Fiero and its approx.43/57 fr/r weight distribution beats the top of the line 911 (996) with its 37/63 fr/r distribution.  This does not make for better handling all by itself, (believe me, I have driven both) but does play an important role. but........... MID-ENGINE ROCKS ANYWAY!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000004||Greg Piet||09-20-1999||11:17 PM||||BigDaddy, I just said the engine behind the driver.  <BR>I don't want to get you all upset as I know there is a difference between rear and mid engine although I need to be motoring along fairly well for me to notice it.<BR>Besides, I dont have a Porsche nor can I afford one so I dont get much of a chance to compare the two.  Maybe I should try to get a job at road and track magazine. (Wait forget that they dont have a Fiero in their motor pool) ||||reg||7
Z||000005||88 Fiero||09-20-1999||11:28 PM||||Like I said a Fiero is a poorman's Ferrari....||||reg||10
Z||000006||PaUL||09-21-1999||05:21 AM||||I prefer cars with rear wheel drive and the fiero is one of the few remaining examples. I dont care so much for it being mid engined, sometimes I wish I had a backseat. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||09-21-1999||10:59 AM||||Mid engine is the only way to go....I have been fortunate to drive many different types of cars, many have their own mystique, but few have a Mid engine's comfort and feel!||||reg||14
Z||000008||BlackGT||09-21-1999||11:04 AM||||I too am a Porsche fan BIG TIME! but I can`t afford one. The main reason I bought my Fiero<BR>is that exhaust note! The second reason is that fact that it only has 2 seats! Who needs<BR>a back seat....just have to put up with anoying distractions like heads in your rear view , extra weight and the mrs wanting you to go grocery shopping! Who needs that besides they are just too much fun to drive never mind the fact that they attract all kinds of attention from the opposite sex!!!!||||reg||6
